From 35aa9e6333a38f524c05d0d38b7f59c7174984cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:01:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 074/147] hydra: credit Ben Houston at the top of the MaterialX
 translation

The MaterialX translation follows Ben Houston's blender-materialx-importer (MIT):
it is the reference for what to port to Cycles and how, and its list of
categories was the first grid of the coverage measurement. The exact MaterialX
noises and the hexagonal-tiled image that this translation targets are the
Cycles part of his Blender PR #158054 (Apache 2.0), ported by patch 0025.

None of this was said in the code. It is now written where someone reading the
translation will find it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/material.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hydra/material.cpp b/src/hydra/material.cpp
index 150f4301..06437830 100644
--- a/src/hydra/material.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/material.cpp
@@ -270,6 +270,23 @@ namespace {
  * be removable in one piece: once Cycles understands MaterialX natively, the
  * translation is no longer needed and the "mtlx" render context can be dropped.
  * Keep it self-contained.
+ *
+ * Credits. The translation follows Ben Houston's blender-materialx-importer
+ * (https://github.com/bhouston/blender-materialx-importer, MIT licence,
+ * Copyright (c) 2026 Ben Houston), a validated MaterialX importer for Blender:
+ * it is the reference for which MaterialX nodes to carry over to Cycles and
+ * how, and its list of supported node categories was the first checklist of
+ * the coverage work, before tools/mtlx_coverage.py measured against the whole
+ * MaterialX library. The translation itself is
+ * written in C++ against this delegate's mapping machinery; what it owes the
+ * importer is the map of the ground.
+ *
+ * The MaterialX-exact procedural noise and hex-tiled image nodes this block
+ * targets (mx_noise_texture, mx_hextiled_image_texture) are his too: they are
+ * the Cycles side of his Blender pull request #158054
+ * (https://projects.blender.org/blender/blender/pulls/158054, Apache 2.0),
+ * validated against the MaterialX reference renderer by his material-fidelity
+ * suite, and carried in this series as a patch.
  * ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 
